      "category": "Text",
      "text": "WHEREAS, the City's Consumer Affairs Commissioner has issued a\npreliminary report which, among other things, concludes that there is significant reason to\nbelieve that premiums presently paid by the City's residents for comprehensive automobile\ninsurance do not reflect the dramatic reduction in the risk of auto theft that the City has\nexperienced over the last five years; and",
